14. The following points that arises for my consideration are as under;
1. Whether the Petitioner prove that they were subjected to Domestic Violence by the respondents?
2. Whether the petitioner is entitled for the reliefs as sought in the petition?

On perusal of materials before this court, my findings on the above points are as follows;
Point No.1 : In the affirmative;
Point No.2 : Partly in the affirmative;
Point No.3 : As per final order for the following;
REASONS 16. Point No.1 : In a domestic violence case the petitioner has to prove the domestic relationship between herself and respondent, she was residing with the respondent in a shared household, the domestic violence was caused by the respondent upon her.

45. Point No.3 :- In view of the materials placed before this court, pleadings, deposition and documentary evidence this court proceeds to pass the following;
G.U.Lakshmivishnuvardhana vs Dr.B.S Vishnuvardhana on 9 January, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/133112135/
17  ORDER  The petition filed by the petitioner  under Sec.12 of The Protection of Women  Crl.Misc.157/2012  from Domestic Violence Act, 2005 is  hereby allowed in part.
